WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.724 --> 00:00:16.514
"I have to get to the Metro City Convention Center," thought Roxy.

2
00:00:16.534 --> 00:00:19.496
"I need to find out who stole the jewels!"

3
00:00:20.637 --> 00:00:21.737
Roxy looked at her friends.

4
00:00:21.757 --> 00:00:26.541
"I'll be back soon," she said.

5
00:00:26.561 --> 00:00:28.862
"I just remembered something.

6
00:00:29.783 --> 00:00:31.004
I forgot to walk my dog!"

7
00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.401
"Okay," said Terrell.

8
00:00:33.421 --> 00:00:36.523
"See you in a little—" Roxy ran off.

9
00:00:42.427 --> 00:00:44.108
Roxy arrived at the Convention Center.

10
00:00:45.189 --> 00:00:46.410
She saw a crowd of people.

11
00:00:46.970 --> 00:00:47.791
They looked upset.

12
00:00:48.791 --> 00:00:50.372
All of the jewelry cases were empty.

13
00:00:51.913 --> 00:00:52.654
"Rocket Girl!"

14
00:00:52.834 --> 00:00:54.915
Detective Smith called when he saw Roxy.

15
00:00:59.038 --> 00:00:59.739
glad you're here."

16
00:01:00.879 --> 00:01:01.640
Roxy smiled.

17
00:01:02.284 --> 00:01:04.466
"What are you doing here, Detective?

18
00:01:05.406 --> 00:01:07.087
Shopping for a diamond ring?"

19
00:01:07.107 --> 00:01:10.589
"Ha-ha." Detective Smith pretended to laugh.

20
00:01:10.609 --> 00:01:13.411
"This is serious, Rocket Girl.

21
00:01:14.252 --> 00:01:16.793
Someone stole a lot of valuable jewels."

22
00:01:16.813 --> 00:01:19.575
"I know," said Roxy.

23
00:01:19.595 --> 00:01:21.656
"Have you found any clues?"

24
00:01:21.676 --> 00:01:24.238
"No," said Detective Smith.

25
00:01:24.258 --> 00:01:27.340
"But this wasn't the only robbery tonight.

26
00:01:28.232 --> 00:01:32.214
Jewels were also stolen from the party at the Metro City Grand Hotel."

27
00:01:32.234 --> 00:01:35.876
"Hmm," said Roxy.

28
00:01:35.896 --> 00:01:38.198
"Maybe it's the same thieves.

29
00:01:39.098 --> 00:01:40.779
Jewels were stolen both times."

30
00:01:40.799 --> 00:01:44.061
"Yes!" said a man.

31
00:01:44.081 --> 00:01:47.723
"Very valuable jewels.

32
00:01:48.623 --> 00:01:52.525
Those horrible thieves stole my entire collection of rare emeralds!"

33
00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:55.827
"They took my ruby earrings!"

34
00:01:56.167 --> 00:01:56.968
said a tall woman.

35
00:01:58.096 --> 00:02:00.258
"And my diamond sunglasses!"

36
00:02:00.598 --> 00:02:02.079
said an old woman with blue hair.

37
00:02:03.561 --> 00:02:04.161
She sniffed.

38
00:02:04.181 --> 00:02:08.284
"They were my favorite sunglasses."

39
00:02:08.304 --> 00:02:10.987
"Can anyone tell us what happened?"

40
00:02:11.247 --> 00:02:12.148
asked Detective Smith.

41
00:02:13.028 --> 00:02:14.810
He took a small notebook out of his pocket.

42
00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:17.492
"Did any of you see anything?"

43
00:02:18.613 --> 00:02:20.014
The tall woman stepped forward.

44
00:02:20.034 --> 00:02:23.377
"I didn't see anything," she said.

45
00:02:23.397 --> 00:02:27.180
"But I heard something—a loud rumble.

46
00:02:28.168 --> 00:02:30.189
It sounded like a bunch of motorcycles."

47
00:02:30.209 --> 00:02:33.610
"I heard the rumble too," said the man.

48
00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:36.592
"Then I heard a zapping sound."

49
00:02:36.612 --> 00:02:40.453
"There was a bolt of electricity," his wife added.

50
00:02:41.474 --> 00:02:42.554
"Next the lights went out.

51
00:02:43.455 --> 00:02:46.456
When the lights came back on, all the jewels were gone!"

52
00:02:48.317 --> 00:02:52.078
"The thieves even took my brand-new diamond tiara," said another woman.

53
00:02:52.098 --> 00:02:55.860
"I was going to wear it to the exhibit tomorrow!"

54
00:02:57.056 --> 00:02:57.797
"What exhibit?"

55
00:02:58.017 --> 00:02:58.677
asked Roxy.

56
00:02:58.697 --> 00:03:01.079
"You don't know?"

57
00:03:01.539 --> 00:03:02.740
said the woman with blue hair.

58
00:03:03.581 --> 00:03:04.561
She looked surprised.

59
00:03:04.581 --> 00:03:09.965
"The crown jewels will be on display at the Metro City Museum."

60
00:03:09.985 --> 00:03:13.888
"The crown jewels are magnificent," said the man.

61
00:03:13.908 --> 00:03:17.070
"They just arrived in Metro City today.

62
00:03:18.011 --> 00:03:20.673
And tomorrow the exhibit will be open to the public.

63
00:03:21.593 --> 00:03:25.096
It's the biggest, most valuable collection of jewels in the world."

64
00:03:26.548 --> 00:03:27.410
Roxy gasped.

65
00:03:29.032 --> 00:03:33.499
"I know what the jewel thieves are going to steal next—the crown jewels!"
